  "text": "Recipe: Sprouted Ragi Bread\nCreator: Mrs N K Manku\nCategory: Bread\nIngredients: sprouted ragi flour, flaxseed powder, chia seed powder, date paste, baking powder, baking soda, cinnamon powder, warm peanut milk, plant based milk, warm water, vanilla, nuts, seeds, lemon juice, vinegar, sesame seeds\nCooking methods: bake, air-fry\nInstructions: BATTER: Mix dry ingredients together. Then add warm plant-based milk and water slowly and keep mixing all the ingredients. If needed, add some more plant-based milk or water. Optionally add some ground or chopped nuts or seeds. Then add 1 tsp lemon juice or vinegar.\nBAKE: Transfer batter to a baking container lined with parchment paper. Sprinkle some sesame seeds on top. Bake for 20 to 25 minutes at 180 C in a preheated oven or an air fryer.\nNotes: A recipe with WHOLE GRAINS (sprouted ragi flour), NUTS & SEEDS (flaxseed powder, chia seed powder, peanut milk), SWEETENER (date paste)",
